Ralph Bishop is a heavily scarred, golden-scaled lizardfolk who wears a tailored but slightly too-tight silk waistcoat. He has lost an eye, carries an ornate rapier, and has the manner of a fighter who has been at it far longer than one life.

Ralph Bishop is a member of [[Org/The Scale/index|The Scale]], a senior overseer and the head of the troop of Scale delvers who came to the pilgrimage. He was once the assistant to a seer, on expeditions starward and voidward after disruptions in the weave, and one of those expeditions may have returned with word of [[Phenomena/Hearts|hearts]] made by some means other than the usual. He hears no [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] himself.

He runs the Scale's forward base on the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], a squat concrete outpost with a turning sonar dish on its roof, from which the troop means to map the strider layer by layer. He is a friend of [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/People/Paavo Karhu|Paavo Karhu]] and offered the Party the order's help and a place in its network of hearts.
